summary:
  The retry budget applies to a wake-up too, so an alarm whose station dies
  gives up three knocks later and the sleeper stays asleep.

history:
  The budget was added because a station that has gone away should not be
  knocked at for an hour — issue #13, 2026-09. It is the second refusal on
  this road, after the switch of 2026.37, and it arrives with exactly the
  trap the switch did: a new reason to stop that quietly forgets the one
  order that must never stop. An alarm hands the later death of its station
  to the heal road, so an exemption dropped here means 7:00 becomes silence
  at 7:03 — and nobody would connect an alarm failing to a setting about
  ordinary listening. The exemption is tested ahead of the switch on
  purpose: it has to win over both.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RetryLogic.js

find:
    if (exempt === true) return true;

replace:
    if (exempt === false) return true;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_retrylogic.qml::test_an_alarm_is_bound_by_neither_the_switch_nor_the_budget.
  Also by tests/qml/tst_alarmengine.qml::test_a_firing_alarm_outlives_a_spent_retry_budget,
  which fires a real alarm and feeds its own flag to the real decision.
  Line-neutral.
